This directory builds a link-time stub of `librealsense2.so`.

The DS3D RealSense dataloader (`ds3d/dataloader/realsense`) is built against the
Intel RealSense SDK, but that SDK is not a build dependency of DeepStream. The
stub lets the dataloader link on a machine where the RealSense SDK is not
installed: `librealsense2.export` lists the symbols the dataloader references,
and the Makefile turns each entry into an empty `void sym() {}` definition
before linking them into a shared library with the correct soname.

The stub is a build helper only — `make install` deliberately installs nothing.
At run time the dynamic loader resolves `librealsense2.so` to the real Intel
RealSense SDK, which must be installed on the target for the dataloader to
actually capture from a RealSense camera. See the Intel RealSense SDK
installation guide:
https://github.com/IntelRealSense/librealsense/blob/master/doc/distribution_linux.md

The matching RealSense headers are vendored under `ds3d/3rdparty/realsense2`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- A C compiler (gcc); no external libraries are needed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling this stub:
- Run make
  $ make
- Verify `librealsense2.so` exist in this directory. It is picked up through
  `-L../../stub/realsense` when `ds3d/dataloader/realsense` is linked.

NOTE: Do not install this library into the DeepStream lib directory — it would
shadow the real librealsense2 at run time.
